      "extract": "A natural question arises: *how to choose parameters which describe the shape of a Young diagram in the most convenient way?* A very interesting answer for this question was proposed by Biane [@Biane1998] who for a (generalized) Young diagram $\\lambda$ defined a family of parameters $R_2^{\\lambda},R_3^{\\lambda},\\dots$, called *free cumulants* of $\\lambda$. The original definition of free cumulants of $\\lambda$ given",
      "extractCut": true
    },
