      "extract": "We define the *free cumulants* $R_2^\\lambda,R_3^\\lambda,\\dots$ as $$R_{k}^\\lambda = \\lim_{s\\to\\infty} \\frac{1}{s^{k}} \\Sigma^{s\\lambda}_{k-1},$$ in other words each free cumulant is asymptotically the dominant term of the character on a cycle of appropriate length in the limit when the Young diagram tends to infinity. One of the reasons why free cumulants are so useful in asymptotic representation theory is that",
