      "extract": "It turns out that free cumulants can be used not only to provide asymptotic approximations for the characters of symmetric groups, but also for exact formulas. Kerov during a talk in Institut Henri Poincaré in January 2000 [@Kerov2000talk] announced the following result (the first published proof was given by Biane [@Biane2003]): for each permutation $\\pi$ there exists a unique universal polynomial $K_{\\pi}$ with",
